# DL1: DEEP-CONTEXT arm B of AB (see DA1): the Lever N traffic profile on the window image, the same tests, started right after DA1 so the pair shares the day and the host load. Eight cold 120k arrivals at once are
# also the heaviest robustness shape of the lever (eight splitters in the runner's persistent batch, the deadline governor binding). READ as DA1; a hang, a refusal or a TTFT of the first user over 240 s is a FINDING.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the third session of 2026-10-08/09 (s0809) (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the boxes, the tags
# and every rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11 is the window image (the Lever N traffic profile baked in as its default); tp4-serve-10 is the production base image. C2_BOX_MINUTES is the job's box:
# the workflow enforces it from inside, it never cancels a run. NO profile of this pack carries a digest or an audit (QWEN_PREFIX_DIGESTS, QWEN_PREFIX_AUDIT, the lever audits): test_tp4_session_0809 pins that.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k
C2_BOX_MINUTES=30
